# CONFIG_NOTES

Configuration notes for the Snowflake MoE (CellMoE) project.

## Recommended Environment

- OS: Windows 11 / Linux (Ubuntu 20.04+)
- Python: 3.10+
- GPU: NVIDIA with CUDA 12.8+ recommended (RTX 5060 Laptop tested)
- PyTorch: >= 2.1.0 (CUDA build)

## Key Design

- Fine-grained experts + shared expert (memory point) + sparse top-k activation
- Routing: learned (trainable gate), rules-based, or fixed baselines
- Memory slots are decoupled from routing weights; erasable at inference
- Data: TinyStories / Shakespeare / Bible / MNIST subsets (see data loader in each run script)

## Training Config

- TinyStories runs: 5 epochs, seq len 256, batch as in scripts, LR ~1e-3 with cosine schedule
- MNIST runs: 30 epochs, learned gate with reward events
- Lifelong: sequential domain addition with fixed memory; measure regression on old domain

## Outputs

- All experiment results are logged to `output/results_*.csv`
- Figures (PNG) are also written to `output/`
- Early/experimental scripts are archived under `early_experiments/` (not part of the stable pipeline)

## Red Lines

- Checkpoints, raw data, logs, and *.pt weights are NOT committed to the repository.
